1
00:00:23,666 --> 00:00:26,875
Yeah. That dress
really is perfect, isn't it?

2
00:00:27,666 --> 00:00:28,791
Mm.

3
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:32,666
Ichito, don't you agree?

4
00:00:33,708 --> 00:00:36,375
Your mother always looks
so beautiful in white.

5
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,208
She's been like this
for several years now.

6
00:02:13,375 --> 00:02:15,708
The odds of her regaining consciousness,

7
00:02:17,041 --> 00:02:18,416
are pretty low, right?

8
00:02:19,291 --> 00:02:20,291
Right.

9
00:02:21,791 --> 00:02:23,916
Unfortunately, what happened was

10
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,791
the blood flow to her brain was cut off,
causing severe damage.

11
00:02:27,875 --> 00:02:31,750
And, sadly,
we aren't expecting any improvement.

12
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:36,416
Use the call button
if you need help with anything.

13
00:02:55,541 --> 00:02:56,750
I, uh…

14
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:01,541
…wish I'd come to see her sooner.

15
00:03:04,875 --> 00:03:06,375
It wouldn't have mattered.

16
00:03:21,541 --> 00:03:23,208
Professor Toyohara.

17
00:03:31,875 --> 00:03:34,208
I never thought you'd come here.

18
00:03:36,458 --> 00:03:37,791
I got careless.

19
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:42,083
Professor, why are you here?

20
00:03:45,875 --> 00:03:49,625
Your father and I were best friends,
back in university.

21
00:03:51,791 --> 00:03:54,000
But slowly, we drifted apart.

22
00:03:55,875 --> 00:03:58,291
Believe it or not,
I even changed your diaper.

23
00:04:02,166 --> 00:04:03,833
After that whole thing happened,

24
00:04:04,708 --> 00:04:07,916
I'd come back
to check on your mom occasionally.

25
00:04:08,708 --> 00:04:11,291
So why…

26
00:04:12,208 --> 00:04:13,916
didn't you ever tell me anything?

27
00:04:15,666 --> 00:04:19,250
Because I knew very well
that you were avoiding your mother.

28
00:04:21,208 --> 00:04:23,750
I thought having someone around
who knew what you'd been through

29
00:04:24,250 --> 00:04:26,166
would be particularly painful.

30
00:04:29,708 --> 00:04:31,916
I've been extremely hard on you,

31
00:04:32,625 --> 00:04:33,708
and I'm sorry.

32
00:04:35,875 --> 00:04:38,125
I wanted you to be able to move forward,

33
00:04:38,208 --> 00:04:41,583
and I was hoping a sex therapist was
the last thing you'd want to be.

34
00:04:42,166 --> 00:04:44,000
I realize how selfish that was.

35
00:04:52,833 --> 00:04:54,458
<i>It was almost as if</i>

36
00:04:55,875 --> 00:04:58,083
<i>time had stood still.</i>

37
00:05:01,791 --> 00:05:05,583
<i>In my memories,</i>
<i>my mother hadn't changed a bit.</i>

38
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:10,708
<i>Like she was still right there,</i>
<i>in that house.</i>

39
00:05:11,916 --> 00:05:13,333
Your mother…

40
00:05:14,708 --> 00:05:17,000
has no recollection of what happened.

41
00:05:19,541 --> 00:05:20,541
Really?

42
00:05:21,125 --> 00:05:23,083
Likely a dissociative disorder.

43
00:05:24,291 --> 00:05:26,291
I would venture to say that

44
00:05:26,791 --> 00:05:28,958
time has completely frozen for her.

45
00:05:32,083 --> 00:05:33,791
Before she lost consciousness,

46
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:37,791
she would go on and on
about the day your voice changed.

47
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:41,833
Or the time you made her
an omelette for Mother's Day.

48
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:49,208
I was wondering…

49
00:05:50,625 --> 00:05:52,333
Professor, do you have…

50
00:05:54,916 --> 00:05:56,125
any idea…

51
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,041
how something like this
could have happened?

52
00:06:02,625 --> 00:06:04,166
I can't be sure.

53
00:06:07,916 --> 00:06:09,250
But, uh…

54
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:14,208
I did, on occasion,
witness the sort of oppression

55
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:15,833
she was dealing with.

56
00:06:17,958 --> 00:06:19,125
Oppression?

57
00:06:22,875 --> 00:06:26,833
Ichito, your father
was quite a gifted surgeon.

58
00:06:28,666 --> 00:06:31,291
He was also the definition
of a perfectionist.

59
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:36,166
And he expected that kind of perfection…

60
00:06:37,791 --> 00:06:40,750
from all those around him,
including your mother.

61
00:06:42,708 --> 00:06:44,541
He transformed her into a…

62
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:48,583
into a beautiful woman.

63
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:54,333
And what he believed was
the perfect wife and devoted mother.

64
00:06:55,708 --> 00:06:56,916
Everything from

65
00:06:57,916 --> 00:06:59,541
the clothes she wore,

66
00:07:00,166 --> 00:07:02,750
right down to how she styled her hair.

67
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,250
That dress really is the perfect one.

68
00:07:08,625 --> 00:07:09,666
Hm.

69
00:07:10,166 --> 00:07:14,541
Enduring that kind of control
and oppression drove her to the brink.

70
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:19,041
And she had an affair,
just to escape it all.

71
00:07:21,333 --> 00:07:23,875
That sent him into an absolute rage.

72
00:07:24,375 --> 00:07:28,333
But his anger wasn't directed at her.
She was just the doll he had created.

73
00:07:29,166 --> 00:07:31,708
It was focused on the man that…

74
00:07:33,583 --> 00:07:35,833
had taken that doll away from him.

75
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,875
My father had

76
00:07:44,791 --> 00:07:46,583
a Pygmalion complex.

77
00:07:47,208 --> 00:07:49,041
At least, it seems that way.

78
00:07:51,291 --> 00:07:54,625
A Pyg-malion complex?

79
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,583
Basically, what that is

80
00:07:59,083 --> 00:08:01,000
is an obsession with dolls.

81
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:04,833
But, more specifically,

82
00:08:05,333 --> 00:08:10,708
it's a desire to force another person
into an ideal mold and control them.

83
00:08:16,666 --> 00:08:18,041
This whole time,

84
00:08:18,666 --> 00:08:22,125
I thought my mother was
the one with sexual issues.

85
00:08:24,583 --> 00:08:25,583
But, uh…

86
00:08:26,916 --> 00:08:29,583
looks like it was my father
all along who was

87
00:08:30,416 --> 00:08:32,041
the one with the problem.

88
00:08:38,291 --> 00:08:42,916
<i>These eerily named "Ghost Stairs"</i>
<i>are believed to have 40 steps going up,</i>

89
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,250
<i>but only 39 going down.</i>

90
00:08:46,458 --> 00:08:48,416
<i>When you physically walk down,</i>

91
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:51,958
<i>there is a noticeable tilt</i>
<i>on that last step.</i>

92
00:08:53,708 --> 00:08:57,083
<i>So you're saying there is</i>
<i>an obvious tilt on that last step, right?</i>

93
00:08:57,166 --> 00:08:59,291
<i>All right, could you actually</i>
<i>climb those stairs again</i>

94
00:08:59,375 --> 00:09:00,666
<i>so our viewers could see it live?</i>

95
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:02,250
And…

96
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:04,458
Yumi?

97
00:09:06,625 --> 00:09:07,458
<i>Yes?</i>

98
00:09:07,541 --> 00:09:09,375
<i>Everything okay? You need a break?</i>

99
00:09:09,458 --> 00:09:11,750
- Oh, no, I'm fine.
<i>- Ah.</i>

100
00:09:16,416 --> 00:09:18,083
<i>Ms. Ichinose. Morning.</i>

101
00:09:18,166 --> 00:09:19,458
Talk to you a minute?

102
00:09:23,041 --> 00:09:25,041
Future Women Leaders Week?

103
00:09:25,125 --> 00:09:26,166
Mmm.

104
00:09:26,250 --> 00:09:28,416
The program directors
have developed this project

105
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:32,166
in order to modernize
the network's outdated corporate image.

106
00:09:33,250 --> 00:09:36,583
The aim is to run several different
week-long special programs.

107
00:09:36,666 --> 00:09:39,875
And our show is getting pulled
along for the ride.

108
00:09:45,083 --> 00:09:48,000
I know it's looking pretty sparse
at first glance.

109
00:09:48,083 --> 00:09:51,500
Think you and Mitarai can run wiEth it
and come up with a few ideas?

110
00:09:52,291 --> 00:09:53,291
Hmm?

111
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:56,791
Is this for real?

112
00:09:56,875 --> 00:09:58,125
Are you serious?

113
00:09:58,208 --> 00:10:00,416
Ha. That's why I'm asking.

114
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:02,000
Get to it.

115
00:10:02,083 --> 00:10:04,125
Uh, sir?

116
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:06,708
Why'd you ask me?

117
00:10:07,208 --> 00:10:08,208
Hm.

118
00:10:08,833 --> 00:10:11,250
Little bird told me
you were the one for the job.

119
00:10:11,750 --> 00:10:12,875
Good luck!

120
00:10:15,125 --> 00:10:17,583
Morning. Have a good vacation?

121
00:10:22,041 --> 00:10:23,916
Hey! Shun, wait up.

122
00:10:24,875 --> 00:10:26,416
Hey.

123
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,458
You recommended me
for the article, didn't you?

124
00:10:28,541 --> 00:10:30,541
I really do appreciate it!

125
00:10:30,625 --> 00:10:31,625
Huh?

126
00:10:33,208 --> 00:10:34,916
Future Women Leaders Week.

127
00:10:35,625 --> 00:10:38,166
Oh. You're gonna be working on that too?

128
00:10:39,083 --> 00:10:40,958
Uh… Yes.

129
00:10:41,458 --> 00:10:42,958
- Fantastic.
- Ah.

130
00:10:46,375 --> 00:10:49,125
Well, if you need anything,
let me know, all right?

131
00:11:20,291 --> 00:11:23,916
The reason why I asked you
why you chose to deal with sexuality

132
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,875
was out of genuine concern.

133
00:11:26,875 --> 00:11:28,625
Is the work you do now…

134
00:11:30,333 --> 00:11:34,833
<i>actually a profession that you pursued</i>
<i>because you genuinely wanted to?</i>

135
00:11:38,291 --> 00:11:39,625
Doctor?

136
00:11:39,708 --> 00:11:41,500
- Can I talk to you?
- Oh.

137
00:11:41,583 --> 00:11:43,375
Things are getting a bit
out of hand out there.

138
00:11:43,458 --> 00:11:44,875
- Huh?
- Can you have a look?

139
00:11:44,958 --> 00:11:46,333
Thanks.

140
00:11:48,125 --> 00:11:49,250
You see?

141
00:11:51,625 --> 00:11:54,750
Uh… what exactly are you up to?

142
00:11:54,833 --> 00:11:56,708
I figured, since we have no appointments,

143
00:11:56,791 --> 00:11:58,833
I might as well get started
on some dried herbs.

144
00:11:58,916 --> 00:12:00,041
Oh.

145
00:12:00,125 --> 00:12:02,166
Could you bundle a few together for me?

146
00:12:02,250 --> 00:12:04,666
- Three or four stems each.
- Uh… Yeah, sure.

147
00:12:04,750 --> 00:12:07,416
And, Yuta… you get…

148
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:08,375
Huh?

149
00:12:10,125 --> 00:12:11,250
This!

150
00:12:11,333 --> 00:12:12,458
What's this?

151
00:12:18,916 --> 00:12:20,125
Oh!

152
00:12:22,833 --> 00:12:24,125
These smell great.

153
00:12:24,208 --> 00:12:25,291
Yeah.

154
00:12:25,375 --> 00:12:28,541
Herbs keep their fragrance for a while,
even after they've been cut.

155
00:12:28,625 --> 00:12:30,083
Argh! A bug!

156
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:33,250
The scent is so vibrant
when they're nice and fresh.

157
00:12:33,333 --> 00:12:36,458
Then it becomes more mellow
and concentrated when they're dry.

158
00:12:36,541 --> 00:12:39,208
- Oh! Another bug!
- You're ruining the mood!

159
00:12:40,375 --> 00:12:43,083
Just try to… keep it down.

160
00:12:43,166 --> 00:12:44,208
All right?

161
00:12:47,041 --> 00:12:48,041
Sorry.

162
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,916
The fragrance of a flower

163
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,416
will remain in your mind
long after its beauty has wilted.

164
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,166
Hello?

165
00:13:15,083 --> 00:13:16,208
- Ah!
- Ah!

166
00:13:19,083 --> 00:13:22,375
Hi, is it possible to see the doctor,
even if I don't have an appointment?

167
00:13:22,458 --> 00:13:24,666
- Oh. Yes.
- Thank you.

168
00:13:29,458 --> 00:13:30,500
Hello.

169
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:35,458
I… uh…

170
00:13:35,541 --> 00:13:39,041
I attended your lectures
at the university a while ago.

171
00:13:44,875 --> 00:13:45,875
Oh.

172
00:13:48,041 --> 00:13:49,625
Yuka Namioka.

173
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:51,916
Yes.

174
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,666
So, how can I help you, Yuka?

175
00:13:57,750 --> 00:13:59,500
It's probably nothing.

176
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:03,916
And if anyone told me this really wasn't
worth pursuing, I'd most likely drop it.

177
00:14:06,833 --> 00:14:09,208
If this is something
that's bothering you, Yuka,

178
00:14:09,291 --> 00:14:10,916
then it's worth pursuing.

179
00:14:19,666 --> 00:14:21,083
There's a professor,

180
00:14:22,208 --> 00:14:23,541
at the university.

181
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:27,375
The way he looks at me,
it just feels very sexual.

182
00:14:28,208 --> 00:14:31,333
Maybe I'm imagining it, I… I don't know.

183
00:14:31,958 --> 00:14:35,958
Why don't you tell me a little more?

184
00:14:38,666 --> 00:14:41,458
Well, seeing as though
I'm an undergrad student,

185
00:14:41,541 --> 00:14:43,791
I spend a lot of time in the lab
working on projects

186
00:14:43,875 --> 00:14:45,916
in the field I want to specialize in.

187
00:14:46,625 --> 00:14:49,166
This professor was quite easy to talk to.

188
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:53,416
Suddenly, he started taking
a real interest in my research.

189
00:14:53,916 --> 00:14:56,041
Or specifically, an interest in me.

190
00:14:56,708 --> 00:14:59,166
Oh… That sounded really conceited,
didn't it?

191
00:14:59,250 --> 00:15:00,583
I just meant, you know…

192
00:15:00,666 --> 00:15:01,875
Ah.

193
00:15:04,541 --> 00:15:08,333
Then he started inviting me to faculty
dinners and events and things like that.

194
00:15:09,041 --> 00:15:11,666
I was happy about it at first, I admit.

195
00:15:12,875 --> 00:15:17,166
But eventually,
the outings and dinners were more private.

196
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:22,291
Then there were overnight conferences.
And I was the only one he invited.

197
00:15:23,666 --> 00:15:26,291
He never made any physical advances,

198
00:15:26,375 --> 00:15:29,958
and it's not like he asked me
to share a hotel room or anything.

199
00:15:31,333 --> 00:15:35,041
That's why I never felt like
I could tell anyone anything about it.

200
00:15:35,625 --> 00:15:37,916
But it made you feel uncomfortable,

201
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,708
or that he might have wanted you sexually?

202
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:48,625
And when we were, um…
at those conferences,

203
00:15:48,708 --> 00:15:50,208
it always felt like…

204
00:15:51,250 --> 00:15:53,958
more of a couple thing
than student-professor.

205
00:15:54,041 --> 00:15:56,375
It kind of made me feel like an escort.

206
00:15:56,916 --> 00:15:59,541
He even bought me clothes
to wear to all these things.

207
00:16:03,583 --> 00:16:05,916
He'd also invite me to these dessert bars.

208
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:09,041
He said, as an older man,
he felt funny going there alone.

209
00:16:09,958 --> 00:16:12,291
A bizarre man this, uh…

210
00:16:13,458 --> 00:16:14,750
Professor Kurusu.

211
00:16:24,583 --> 00:16:26,000
What do you think of this?

212
00:16:29,625 --> 00:16:30,708
Hmm…

213
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,708
- Think they'll approve it?
- Not sure.

214
00:16:33,791 --> 00:16:36,541
I don't know if it has the hook
Kujo is always looking for.

215
00:16:36,625 --> 00:16:39,750
Yeah, I know.

216
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:42,375
Hey, uh…
Sorry for keeping you here so late.

217
00:16:42,458 --> 00:16:45,291
It's okay. Look, it's a good idea, though.

218
00:16:45,375 --> 00:16:49,208
I think you need to become the kind of
journalist you've always wanted to be.

219
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:51,750
I remember, back in school,

220
00:16:51,833 --> 00:16:54,208
I always thought you'd make
an amazing field reporter.

221
00:16:56,416 --> 00:16:57,833
You thought that?

222
00:16:57,916 --> 00:16:59,666
Aww! Thank you!

223
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:02,500
I'm so happy to be working with you!

224
00:17:03,375 --> 00:17:05,833
So tell me…
You were the one who recommended me

225
00:17:05,916 --> 00:17:07,500
for this project, weren't you?

226
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,416
I really appreciate it.

227
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,416
No. It wasn't me.

228
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:12,833
Huh?

229
00:17:13,958 --> 00:17:15,750
- Huh?
- Huh?

230
00:17:17,083 --> 00:17:19,500
Japan lags far behind in sex education,

231
00:17:19,583 --> 00:17:23,375
and the public's ignorance is
the driving force behind this proposal.

232
00:17:24,708 --> 00:17:26,000
Hmm.

233
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:28,208
Mm. Feels like it's a bit heavy.

234
00:17:30,708 --> 00:17:32,916
To be clear, I'm not against airing this.

235
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
It just needs more of a hook.

236
00:17:35,083 --> 00:17:36,791
- Right.
- Uh… yeah.

237
00:17:36,875 --> 00:17:37,875
- Mm.
- Hm.

238
00:17:37,958 --> 00:17:40,333
Japan ranks especially low
on the Gender Gap Index,

239
00:17:40,416 --> 00:17:43,625
so how about we focus more
on the lack of political participation?

240
00:17:43,708 --> 00:17:45,583
Mm-mm. Mm, no. That's the kind of thing

241
00:17:45,666 --> 00:17:48,041
News One covers
in their 10:00 p.m. segment.

242
00:17:48,125 --> 00:17:49,791
We're an evening news show.

243
00:17:49,875 --> 00:17:52,041
I want to take a more casual approach.

244
00:17:52,125 --> 00:17:54,333
- Okay? Harashima!
- Right. Sorry.

245
00:17:54,416 --> 00:17:55,625
- All good.
- Okay, then…

246
00:17:55,708 --> 00:17:59,083
Does anyone here know what
the Pygmalion complex is?

247
00:18:00,291 --> 00:18:01,250
Pyg-what?

248
00:18:01,333 --> 00:18:03,916
I just actually learned about it myself.

249
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:08,083
It refers to people, mostly men,

250
00:18:08,166 --> 00:18:10,416
who treat their women like dolls.

251
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:13,375
Who try to mold them into
their idea of perfection.

252
00:18:17,416 --> 00:18:19,833
Ironically, where I'm concerned,

253
00:18:19,916 --> 00:18:24,750
I feel like this company and our viewers
have been doing exactly that to me.

254
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:29,041
But I don't think it's necessarily
because I'm a female TV personality.

255
00:18:29,541 --> 00:18:34,125
I think it expands to almost any woman
out there living in this country today.

256
00:18:36,083 --> 00:18:40,125
This society forces expectations
of womanhood onto us.

257
00:18:40,208 --> 00:18:43,375
It robs all women,
and makes us feel like dolls.

258
00:18:43,875 --> 00:18:47,083
- It's especially prevalent with sex--
- Miss Ichinose.

259
00:18:47,166 --> 00:18:50,333
Again, I find that way too serious.

260
00:18:52,458 --> 00:18:54,541
- I agree.
- I just don't know anymore.

261
00:18:54,625 --> 00:18:57,083
- So what's the consensus?
- Wait a minute.

262
00:18:57,166 --> 00:19:01,666
You're saying this will involve
women openly discussing sex?

263
00:19:03,458 --> 00:19:06,708
Yes. Yes, exactly. Exactly right.

264
00:19:06,791 --> 00:19:10,041
I want us to take this opportunity

265
00:19:10,125 --> 00:19:12,833
to tackle the topic of sex head-on.

266
00:19:13,416 --> 00:19:15,541
That's pretty gutsy, I got to admit.

267
00:19:17,041 --> 00:19:19,875
A special feature like this
coming from a female reporter,

268
00:19:19,958 --> 00:19:22,166
I mean, that's exactly
what we're looking for, isn't it?

269
00:19:22,250 --> 00:19:24,500
- It'll be different.
- A welcome change.

270
00:19:24,583 --> 00:19:26,541
From the light, gossipy stuff
we did in the past.

271
00:19:26,625 --> 00:19:28,208
- Sure.
- Don't you think?

272
00:19:28,291 --> 00:19:30,583
- Uh, whew… Let's go for it.
- Definitely has a hook.

273
00:19:31,208 --> 00:19:32,875
- Give it a shot!
- Really?

274
00:19:32,958 --> 00:19:35,916
- Oh, yeah?
- So what do we call it? Anyone?

275
00:19:36,416 --> 00:19:37,958
Any ideas?

276
00:19:38,041 --> 00:19:41,083
How does "So You Want
To Talk About Sex?" sound?

277
00:19:41,708 --> 00:19:43,250
- Catchy!
- I like it.

278
00:19:43,333 --> 00:19:45,208
- Oh, yeah. Great!
- Mitarai.

279
00:19:45,291 --> 00:19:47,541
- Yes.
- You and Miss Ichinose get working on it.

280
00:19:47,625 --> 00:19:48,541
On it.

281
00:19:48,625 --> 00:19:50,750
I'll make sure it's green-lit upstairs.

282
00:19:50,833 --> 00:19:52,500
- All right, let's get to it.
- Great.

283
00:19:52,583 --> 00:19:54,250
- Amazing.
- I'm excited.

284
00:19:54,333 --> 00:19:56,041
- Great!
- You heard the man!

285
00:20:18,916 --> 00:20:21,500
This was all your doing, wasn't it?

286
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,583
Recommending me?

287
00:20:28,958 --> 00:20:29,916
Hmm.

288
00:20:30,416 --> 00:20:31,541
Thank you.

289
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:34,625
Don't thank me.

290
00:20:34,708 --> 00:20:36,708
I just wanted to make the show better.

291
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,833
Yumi, do you remember

292
00:20:43,333 --> 00:20:46,458
the time you and I got an invite
to entertain a sponsor?

293
00:20:47,083 --> 00:20:48,208
Huh?

294
00:20:48,291 --> 00:20:50,250
One of the clients got drunk that night.

295
00:20:50,333 --> 00:20:53,041
He started harassing us
at the karaoke after-party.

296
00:20:54,458 --> 00:20:56,333
Aah.

297
00:20:56,416 --> 00:21:00,750
You discreetly stepped in and diverted
his attention away from me, didn't you?

298
00:21:01,291 --> 00:21:03,750
Just so I wouldn't be the target.

299
00:21:05,333 --> 00:21:06,250
Mmm.

300
00:21:06,750 --> 00:21:08,291
Yeah, I remember.

301
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:14,541
I was, uh…

302
00:21:15,041 --> 00:21:16,833
really pissed off at you.

303
00:21:17,875 --> 00:21:18,791
Huh?

304
00:21:19,291 --> 00:21:21,625
I wanted you to actually say something.

305
00:21:21,708 --> 00:21:24,416
Not just play the victim
and take one for the team.

306
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:26,166
I wanted you to step up.

307
00:21:27,250 --> 00:21:29,208
And while we're at it,

308
00:21:29,833 --> 00:21:32,791
female TV personalities should be
free to date whoever they want.

309
00:21:32,875 --> 00:21:35,125
Why should some old scandal
about a boyfriend's parents

310
00:21:35,208 --> 00:21:37,416
affect how a woman on TV is judged?

311
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,208
I hated seeing you bow to the pressure

312
00:21:39,291 --> 00:21:41,666
and go along with
whatever they expected of you.

313
00:21:47,291 --> 00:21:48,416
Uh…

314
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:50,083
is this funny?

315
00:21:50,750 --> 00:21:52,583
Uh. No. My bad.

316
00:21:58,291 --> 00:21:59,208
Hey.

317
00:22:00,208 --> 00:22:01,500
Let's have dinner.

318
00:22:01,583 --> 00:22:04,250
What? So now
you're trying to be my best friend?

319
00:22:04,333 --> 00:22:06,166
I'm serious. Let's have dinner.

320
00:22:06,250 --> 00:22:07,791
Do you like Italian?

321
00:22:08,375 --> 00:22:10,458
- Rolling.
- Hello, excuse me.

322
00:22:10,541 --> 00:22:14,500
We're asking people today if they have any
concerns related to sex. How about you?

323
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:17,541
And so I've tried to find a partner
on several dating apps.

324
00:22:17,625 --> 00:22:20,958
I apologize, I know it can be awkward
talking about sex. How do you feel about…

325
00:22:21,041 --> 00:22:23,166
…about the lack of openness
when it comes to sex?

326
00:22:23,250 --> 00:22:25,458
- Are you asking in public?
- That's personal!

327
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:30,041
I gotta tell you, I really didn't think
anyone would be willing to talk to us,

328
00:22:30,125 --> 00:22:33,041
but people had way more to say
than I ever could've imagined.

329
00:22:33,125 --> 00:22:34,125
Mmm.

330
00:22:34,208 --> 00:22:36,708
My wife and I don't have sex anymore.

331
00:22:36,791 --> 00:22:38,958
Now I'm thinking it might have
something to do with me.

332
00:22:41,416 --> 00:22:43,291
Don't know if that's true.

333
00:22:43,375 --> 00:22:47,041
But sexual issues can affect men
as well as women.

334
00:22:47,125 --> 00:22:48,375
Hm.

335
00:22:48,458 --> 00:22:50,791
If people have as many
concerns as we think,

336
00:22:50,875 --> 00:22:52,791
we should have a professional
talk about it.

337
00:22:52,875 --> 00:22:53,750
Mmm.

338
00:22:53,833 --> 00:22:56,083
We just gotta find someone
we could interview.

339
00:22:57,250 --> 00:23:00,250
- Oh! What about Furuya?
- Imagine that!

340
00:23:00,333 --> 00:23:02,375
- I don't think so.
- No, then?

341
00:23:02,458 --> 00:23:04,833
<i>Then he said he wanted</i>
<i>to do it without a condom.</i>

342
00:23:04,916 --> 00:23:08,125
<i>What about STDs or getting</i>
<i>pregnant? Does that concern you?</i>

343
00:23:08,208 --> 00:23:10,333
- <i>Yes, it totally does.</i>
- <i>I don't blame you.</i>

344
00:23:10,416 --> 00:23:14,416
<i>My husband and I haven't</i>
<i>had sex in well over two years now,</i>

345
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:17,666
<i>and so I've tried to find a partner</i>
<i>on several different dating apps.</i>

346
00:23:17,750 --> 00:23:19,916
- <i>You don't mind multiple partners?</i>
- Okay.

347
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,041
<i>As long as I'm--</i>

348
00:23:21,541 --> 00:23:23,250
Think it's time to take a little break.

349
00:23:23,333 --> 00:23:24,333
Yes.

350
00:23:31,416 --> 00:23:34,416
- We're just taking a quick break.
- Yeah, of course.

351
00:23:35,666 --> 00:23:36,666
Oh.

352
00:23:39,333 --> 00:23:40,541
How's it going?

353
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:44,208
- Oh, thanks.
- No problem.

354
00:23:45,208 --> 00:23:47,791
Well, the footage is looking good.

355
00:23:47,875 --> 00:23:50,708
Trouble is, we're having
a problem finding a commentator.

356
00:23:50,791 --> 00:23:54,500
Yeah, I can see how
that could be a challenge.

357
00:23:58,500 --> 00:23:59,583
Yumi?

358
00:24:02,375 --> 00:24:04,125
Mind if I ask you something?

359
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:05,833
Sure.

360
00:24:07,500 --> 00:24:10,458
What kind of relationship
do you have with Shun?

361
00:24:11,291 --> 00:24:12,291
What?

362
00:24:13,250 --> 00:24:16,583
Relationship? We're co-workers.
He's senior and I'm junior.

363
00:24:16,666 --> 00:24:18,333
That's not what I mean.

364
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:21,416
What I'm asking is
what you think of him as a man?

365
00:24:23,208 --> 00:24:24,416
Uh…

366
00:24:25,416 --> 00:24:27,958
Um… is it possible
that you're interested in him?

367
00:24:28,041 --> 00:24:31,416
Oh, goodness, no. Not at all.

368
00:24:31,916 --> 00:24:33,583
- I didn't think so.
- Right.

369
00:24:35,458 --> 00:24:38,708
But haven't the two of you
gone for a meal together?

370
00:24:39,833 --> 00:24:42,791
Yeah. That was really
only a work thing, though.

371
00:24:45,125 --> 00:24:46,125
Wait.

372
00:24:46,916 --> 00:24:49,625
Are you saying that he…

373
00:24:50,166 --> 00:24:55,208
That's exactly what I'm saying.
Shun definitely has feelings for you.

374
00:24:56,625 --> 00:24:58,000
Oh, man…

375
00:24:59,083 --> 00:25:00,750
I… I, uh…

376
00:25:03,083 --> 00:25:05,583
- I sure hope not.
- I know, right?

377
00:25:05,666 --> 00:25:08,750
You don't think he'd take advantage
of his position, do you?

378
00:25:08,833 --> 00:25:10,958
I can't believe he'd use
his seniority like that.

379
00:25:11,041 --> 00:25:13,125
- Think that's what he's doing?
- You never know.

380
00:25:13,208 --> 00:25:15,208
Guys like that would stoop to any means

381
00:25:15,291 --> 00:25:18,500
if they thought it could get them
somewhere with a woman.

382
00:25:18,583 --> 00:25:20,125
All I know is that I'm so thankful

383
00:25:20,208 --> 00:25:22,416
that kind of drama isn't happening
on my own show.

384
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:24,125
But I have to admit…

385
00:25:24,208 --> 00:25:26,625
I wasn't sure what was
going on between the two of you.

386
00:25:26,708 --> 00:25:29,416
- Well, let me put that to rest.
- Good!

387
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:30,583
Nothing at all.

388
00:25:30,666 --> 00:25:33,791
Oh, I can't tell you
how relieved I am. Seriously!

389
00:25:35,333 --> 00:25:37,875
I told you, it's just a misunderstanding!

390
00:25:40,333 --> 00:25:44,583
Don't tell me she's saying it's some
kind of sexual or academic harassment?

391
00:25:44,666 --> 00:25:46,125
No.

392
00:25:46,958 --> 00:25:48,666
- But you have--
- Just listen.

393
00:25:49,458 --> 00:25:51,291
She was under no obligation to come.

394
00:25:51,375 --> 00:25:53,666
I never forced her or pressured her.

395
00:25:57,125 --> 00:25:58,583
You have to admit, as a student,

396
00:25:58,666 --> 00:26:00,791
there are benefits
to attending a conference.

397
00:26:01,291 --> 00:26:05,291
And you are clearly
in an influential position as a professor.

398
00:26:10,041 --> 00:26:12,041
If she says no to having lunch,

399
00:26:12,916 --> 00:26:14,666
or doesn't accept a gift,

400
00:26:15,583 --> 00:26:18,875
she'd be worried that
she was upsetting her professor.

401
00:26:18,958 --> 00:26:21,958
And that kind of concern could
already be considered

402
00:26:22,833 --> 00:26:24,041
harassment.

403
00:26:24,791 --> 00:26:25,708
Hmm.

404
00:26:25,791 --> 00:26:29,333
- That girl really didn't seem the type--
- It's not "that girl."

405
00:26:31,083 --> 00:26:33,083
Her name's Yuka Namioka.

406
00:26:36,166 --> 00:26:37,666
Wouldn't you agree

407
00:26:37,750 --> 00:26:42,083
you were putting your own feelings
and assumptions ahead of Yuka's?

408
00:26:42,166 --> 00:26:44,833
Can you not see why this would
put her in an awkward position?

409
00:26:46,791 --> 00:26:48,291
And by doing that,

410
00:26:48,833 --> 00:26:52,333
can you not see you were treating her
like your own personal doll?

411
00:26:58,416 --> 00:27:00,500
My father did that exact thing.

412
00:27:02,333 --> 00:27:04,625
He never considered my mother's feelings.

413
00:27:06,791 --> 00:27:09,541
He insisted on pushing
his ideal image on her.

414
00:27:11,875 --> 00:27:13,166
And because of that,

415
00:27:14,208 --> 00:27:16,333
my mother suffered terribly.

416
00:27:16,833 --> 00:27:18,833
The whole time they were together.

417
00:27:21,458 --> 00:27:23,750
All right, but that has nothing
to do with me, though.

418
00:27:25,541 --> 00:27:26,541
No.

419
00:27:27,958 --> 00:27:29,583
It doesn't, but back then,

420
00:27:30,208 --> 00:27:32,208
there was really nothing I could do.

421
00:27:34,250 --> 00:27:35,416
But now…

422
00:27:36,458 --> 00:27:41,291
Now I know I have the opportunity to help
someone else in the same situation.

423
00:27:48,750 --> 00:27:52,000
You can make things right.
It's not too late.

424
00:28:00,500 --> 00:28:02,208
Why not give therapy a shot?

425
00:28:03,666 --> 00:28:05,333
I know I can help you.

426
00:28:08,791 --> 00:28:11,166
Ah. You give me no choice.

427
00:28:11,250 --> 00:28:12,791
I could never say no to you.

428
00:28:17,125 --> 00:28:19,375
Thank you. You won't regret this.

429
00:28:43,875 --> 00:28:45,750
Hello, Yumi? It's me.

430
00:28:47,166 --> 00:28:48,125
<i>Hi.</i>

431
00:28:49,625 --> 00:28:50,750
So, uh…

432
00:28:53,166 --> 00:28:55,000
I need to tell you something.

433
00:29:16,541 --> 00:29:19,250
So, uh, how's your mom doing?

434
00:29:20,458 --> 00:29:22,666
She seems stable, thanks for asking.

435
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:27,833
But she still hasn't regained
consciousness at all.

436
00:29:30,083 --> 00:29:31,250
I'm sorry.

437
00:29:52,625 --> 00:29:54,000
So I, uh…

438
00:29:54,083 --> 00:29:56,250
I wanted to tell you something,
but now, uh…

439
00:29:56,333 --> 00:29:58,666
I'm having trouble
finding the words to say it.

440
00:30:01,541 --> 00:30:03,750
Don't worry. Take your time.

441
00:30:10,375 --> 00:30:13,625
As soon as you feel like talking,
I'm listening.

442
00:30:19,458 --> 00:30:20,541
Hmm.

443
00:30:39,166 --> 00:30:40,333
So I, um…

444
00:30:41,166 --> 00:30:44,750
I chose to pursue this profession
as a means of making up for…

445
00:30:45,375 --> 00:30:47,000
for shunning my parents.

446
00:30:48,541 --> 00:30:50,166
So, there it is.

447
00:30:53,083 --> 00:30:55,166
Professor Toyohara asked me,

448
00:30:57,708 --> 00:31:02,333
"Are you doing this job because you want
to, or because you feel you have to?"

449
00:31:06,750 --> 00:31:09,166
Even if it was for redemption,

450
00:31:10,375 --> 00:31:12,791
it's still amazing that so many people

451
00:31:13,333 --> 00:31:14,916
got help because of you.

452
00:31:24,500 --> 00:31:25,666
That's why…

453
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:29,166
I've thought it over
and I want to choose again.

454
00:31:32,791 --> 00:31:36,500
Except this time, I wanna choose it

455
00:31:37,375 --> 00:31:39,208
because I really want to do it.

456
00:31:42,416 --> 00:31:44,208
Not as a means of redemption.

457
00:31:47,833 --> 00:31:49,250
But commit to it.

458
00:31:51,791 --> 00:31:53,291
To all those people.

459
00:31:54,416 --> 00:31:55,916
And to my parents.

460
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:04,541
And also to myself.

461
00:32:10,291 --> 00:32:12,083
I think Marin said it best.

462
00:32:13,291 --> 00:32:15,208
The fragrance of a flower

463
00:32:15,708 --> 00:32:19,958
will remain in your mind
long after its beauty has wilted.

464
00:32:23,375 --> 00:32:24,375
Hmm.

465
00:32:32,416 --> 00:32:34,625
Can I ask you something now, Ichito?

466
00:32:39,125 --> 00:32:40,083
Hmm.

467
00:32:50,458 --> 00:32:51,541
I, uh…

468
00:32:53,375 --> 00:32:55,833
I would really love
for you to be on my show.

469
00:32:58,125 --> 00:32:59,000
What?

470
00:33:01,250 --> 00:33:02,791
Turns out, uh…

471
00:33:03,375 --> 00:33:05,833
sex is pretty hard to discuss.

472
00:33:06,833 --> 00:33:08,958
And there are so many people out there

473
00:33:09,541 --> 00:33:11,375
who have no one to listen to them.

474
00:33:13,208 --> 00:33:14,208
But, uh…

475
00:33:16,250 --> 00:33:18,166
There are people like you, Ichito,

476
00:33:19,125 --> 00:33:21,708
who will listen to their problems
and try to help.

477
00:33:22,291 --> 00:33:23,958
And they should know that.

478
00:33:30,333 --> 00:33:31,875
Will you come on the show?

479
00:33:39,875 --> 00:33:42,583
So tell me, how's he doing now?

480
00:33:43,541 --> 00:33:46,750
Ask him yourself.
You don't need to go through me anymore.

481
00:33:46,833 --> 00:33:48,916
Now that everything's out in the open.

482
00:33:50,041 --> 00:33:52,666
It's not that simple.
He won't open up to me now.

483
00:33:54,750 --> 00:33:59,625
Funny, but I seem to remember you dumping
him on me and asking if I could help him.

484
00:34:00,125 --> 00:34:02,833
You didn't mind being
the bad guy for that.

485
00:34:03,500 --> 00:34:05,250
You were having fun with it too.

486
00:34:05,333 --> 00:34:06,750
Of course I was.

487
00:34:06,833 --> 00:34:09,833
I got to have a front-row
seat to a romance reality show.

488
00:34:09,916 --> 00:34:11,250
Who wouldn't want that?

489
00:34:12,500 --> 00:34:14,916
<i>Stay tuned for a CTV special.</i>

490
00:34:16,791 --> 00:34:19,958
<i>- Tomorrow, only on Central Television.</i>
- Think he can put this behind him?

491
00:34:20,041 --> 00:34:23,458
<i>- Don't miss Twilight News at 4:45 p.m.</i>
- Just her mere existence…

492
00:34:23,916 --> 00:34:27,125
<i>- The special "Future Women Leaders."</i>
- A reason to face his past, move forward.

493
00:34:27,208 --> 00:34:30,791
<i>The first guest will be sex therapist</i>
<i>Dr. Ichito Shimotori.</i>

494
00:34:30,875 --> 00:34:34,541
<i>We'll be discussing sexual issues</i>
<i>that are often hard to talk about.</i>

495
00:34:36,958 --> 00:34:39,208
<i>- At 7:00 p.m…</i>
- Boy, Yumi really went for it, huh?

496
00:34:39,291 --> 00:34:42,083
<i>…young women zookeepers</i>
<i>that are leading us into the future.</i>

497
00:34:42,916 --> 00:34:46,500
<i>We'll also take a look at the incredible</i>
<i>behaviour of some of these animals.</i>

498
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:52,416
I just got the results
of my annual physical.

499
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:54,083
- Oh, yeah?
- There were a couple of issues.

500
00:34:54,166 --> 00:34:56,208
- Oh! Everything okay?
- Yeah, yeah I'm fine.

501
00:34:56,291 --> 00:34:57,708
- Ah.
- But I still have to be careful.

502
00:34:57,791 --> 00:34:59,500
- We gotta take care of ourselves.
- Yeah.

503
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:01,625
And, after the commercial break,

